       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum recommended metformin dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and a dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe dose may be a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and total daily amounts. These are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day total.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common standard regimens.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note."
