     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. 5,100 mg/day of metformin is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no clinical situation where it's appropriate. It would add risk without adding glycemic benefit, and the main danger is lactic acidosis. You've confirmed the dose, but you haven't given a clinical rationale, so I'd rather not put it into the system.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day.\n\nIf you do need a dose above the maximum, please talk with pharmacy or the attending first. They can enter or verify the order through the hospital's override process."
